1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,000
A sound soul dwells within a sound mind and a sound body.

2
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:19,000
Joma, Joma Dabarasa.

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Joma, Joma Dabarasa.

4
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:31,000
As Grand Witch I now declare this witch's mass open, let us begin.

5
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Joma, Joma Dabarasa.

6
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Crona, Ragnarok, come along.

7
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:41,000
Yes, ma'am, Lady Medusa.

8
00:00:53,000 --> 00:01:01,000
Yes, ma'am.

9
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:07,000
Anyway, this is your power!

10
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:07,240
Connect with the...

11
00:01:07,240 --> 00:01:35,540
We must numb our heart

12
00:01:35,540 --> 00:02:05,520
Thank you.

13
00:02:05,540 --> 00:02:23,240
Hold on a moment.

14
00:02:23,380 --> 00:02:24,500
Oh, dear.

15
00:02:24,840 --> 00:02:27,000
What's happening? She won't let us go.

16
00:02:27,420 --> 00:02:29,720
I don't think I know how to deal with this situation.

17
00:02:29,820 --> 00:02:32,460
You can deal with it by shutting up and giving me all your money.

18
00:02:33,740 --> 00:02:35,380
Good evening, Erica Frog.

19
00:02:35,540 --> 00:02:36,640
Did you need something?

20
00:02:37,040 --> 00:02:37,480
Ribbit.

21
00:02:38,260 --> 00:02:40,300
I think you know why I'm stopping you.

22
00:02:40,860 --> 00:02:41,420
Oh, yes.

23
00:02:41,940 --> 00:02:45,880
But come on, it's not as if I'm the only one who brought non-witches to the gathering tonight.

24
00:02:46,280 --> 00:02:50,580
Over there, that little witch is accompanied by a human, so you see it's not just me.

25
00:02:51,860 --> 00:02:54,960
The purity of the witch's mass certainly has gone downhill.

26
00:02:55,440 --> 00:02:58,080
But that isn't what I wanted to talk to you about tonight, Medusa.

27
00:02:58,400 --> 00:02:59,900
I have some questions for you.

28
00:03:00,180 --> 00:03:03,400
First, what were you doing stealing something from the Grand Witch's room?

29
00:03:03,400 --> 00:03:07,520
And second, you snuck yourself onto the staff at the DWMA.

30
00:03:07,940 --> 00:03:09,540
Why in the world would you do that?

31
00:03:10,440 --> 00:03:11,800
Krona, give me my coat.

32
00:03:12,060 --> 00:03:13,380
Yes, right away, Lady Medusa.

33
00:03:17,700 --> 00:03:21,380
My research at the Academy has been fully approved, as you well know.

34
00:03:21,860 --> 00:03:24,060
The Grand Witch herself is on my side, Erika.

35
00:03:26,760 --> 00:03:27,520
Just a minute.

36
00:03:28,240 --> 00:03:29,980
The Grand Witch's eyesight is failing.

37
00:03:30,460 --> 00:03:32,800
She doesn't see what a nuisance you've made of yourself lately.

38
00:03:33,400 --> 00:03:35,720
That Academy is there to hunt down witches.

39
00:03:35,900 --> 00:03:37,200
You know that as well as I do.

40
00:03:37,680 --> 00:03:40,860
If you slip up just once, you won't be the only one in trouble.

41
00:03:40,960 --> 00:03:42,240
You'll take us down with you.

42
00:03:42,980 --> 00:03:44,000
And then there's him.

43
00:03:44,360 --> 00:03:48,160
Why would you try to create a Kishin that could potentially be an enemy to our kind?

44
00:03:48,620 --> 00:03:50,100
You've taken it too far.

45
00:03:50,360 --> 00:03:51,480
It's time for you to starve.

46
00:03:51,480 --> 00:03:56,920
You meddlesome little frog and mouse.

47
00:03:57,300 --> 00:03:59,220
I think I'm going to have to punish you.

48
00:04:01,860 --> 00:04:03,460
Perhaps not right now, though.

49
00:04:03,560 --> 00:04:04,320
I'm in a hurry.

50
00:04:04,900 --> 00:04:08,160
With so many students to look after, the school nurse mustn't be late.

51
00:04:09,160 --> 00:04:10,780
Joma joma davarasa.

52
00:04:10,780 --> 00:04:15,280
I can't stand that witch, stupid snake woman.

53
00:04:21,280 --> 00:04:23,060
Courage that beats out fear.

54
00:04:23,460 --> 00:04:25,220
Maka Albarn's great resolution?

55
00:04:30,420 --> 00:04:31,760
Turn around for me.

56
00:04:32,420 --> 00:04:33,960
And tell me how you've been feeling.

57
00:04:34,480 --> 00:04:36,020
More or less normal, I guess.

58
00:04:36,020 --> 00:04:40,360
Except for lately, I've been having this really weird dream over and over again.

59
00:04:40,980 --> 00:04:42,580
A strange dream, you say?

60
00:04:43,060 --> 00:04:43,380
Yeah.

61
00:04:44,520 --> 00:04:47,700
And it's been bothering me because I can remember it so clearly.

62
00:04:48,700 --> 00:04:51,820
I always start out in this room that's pitch black.

63
00:04:54,760 --> 00:04:58,560
There's a record player, and it's always skipping like the record's scratched or something.

64
00:04:59,180 --> 00:05:04,440
The music that's playing is some kind of jazz song that I think I've heard before but can't really place.

65
00:05:04,440 --> 00:05:09,980
After I've been sitting there for a bit, this guy always appears from the other side of the room.

66
00:05:10,600 --> 00:05:15,020
He's a little demon wearing a fancy suit and dancing this weird dance out of time with the music.

67
00:05:16,420 --> 00:05:18,240
Swing, swing, swing.

68
00:05:18,520 --> 00:05:20,760
Dude, this is jazz. It isn't swing music.

69
00:05:21,140 --> 00:05:23,840
But jazz is so much more appropriate for nighttime.

70
00:05:24,400 --> 00:05:27,020
Far as I know, music's not picky about when it gets played.

71
00:05:27,240 --> 00:05:28,980
You can decide, so why not listen to swing?

72
00:05:29,260 --> 00:05:32,060
That's right. The decision's mine. Yes, sir.

73
00:05:32,060 --> 00:05:34,560
You can decide, too. You're eligible.

74
00:05:36,020 --> 00:05:40,160
When you were cut open like a fish being gutted, you must have been afraid, am I right?

75
00:05:40,820 --> 00:05:44,960
And wouldn't it be nice to have a strong mind, one that can get rid of the fear you feel?

76
00:05:45,620 --> 00:05:48,140
If you forget your fear, you'll become reckless.

77
00:05:49,180 --> 00:05:50,960
That's something they teach at the Academy.

78
00:05:50,960 --> 00:05:54,020
Heh. What kind of fool are you?

79
00:05:54,400 --> 00:05:56,760
Do you think you're in heaven where you can't get hurt again?

80
00:05:57,140 --> 00:05:59,500
Hate to break it to you, but you're still on Earth.

81
00:05:59,720 --> 00:06:03,740
And if you want to stay alive down here, you're going to need more power than you've got now.

82
00:06:04,100 --> 00:06:07,420
Power so overwhelmingly strong, you can say goodbye to all your fears.

83
00:06:07,420 --> 00:06:11,240
You're nothing without that power.

84
00:06:11,480 --> 00:06:13,340
Now come on and get out there already.

85
00:06:13,520 --> 00:06:14,700
Now wait, hold on a second.

86
00:06:15,480 --> 00:06:17,020
Please, I don't want to leave this room.

87
00:06:17,580 --> 00:06:19,980
Let me stay here until the dream is over and I wake up.

88
00:06:20,360 --> 00:06:21,780
I'll even put up with the lame music.

89
00:06:23,080 --> 00:06:24,760
Seek out the power you need.

90
00:06:25,020 --> 00:06:26,240
Find a rule to break.

91
00:06:26,480 --> 00:06:27,740
It will make you stronger.

92
00:06:28,060 --> 00:06:29,960
Stronger, perhaps, than you thought possible.

93
00:06:31,660 --> 00:06:33,980
What makes you so afraid of leaving the room, Sol?

94
00:06:33,980 --> 00:06:40,780
When I leave the room, the darkness continues.

95
00:06:41,440 --> 00:06:44,520
Then all of a sudden I see this light and I move toward it.

96
00:06:44,900 --> 00:06:46,240
But when I go through...

97
00:06:46,240 --> 00:06:50,680
When I go through, I'm coming out of Maka's stomach.

98
00:06:53,700 --> 00:06:54,180
Interesting.

99
00:06:54,560 --> 00:06:58,060
The black blood that's entered his body seems to be having an effect on him.

100
00:06:58,860 --> 00:07:01,520
So, aside from all that, how am I doing?

101
00:07:01,840 --> 00:07:03,680
Well, you still have a slight arrhythmia,

102
00:07:03,680 --> 00:07:06,100
but you seem to be making a nice recovery so far.

103
00:07:06,760 --> 00:07:08,220
Let's just take your blood pressure.

104
00:07:09,400 --> 00:07:11,120
As for this strange dream of yours,

105
00:07:11,300 --> 00:07:13,480
it's not unusual to have recurring nightmares

106
00:07:13,480 --> 00:07:15,400
after going through the trauma that you have.

107
00:07:15,840 --> 00:07:17,260
I don't think you need to be worried.

108
00:07:17,840 --> 00:07:18,400
Is that all?

109
00:07:18,460 --> 00:07:20,240
Or was there something else you've been concerned about?

110
00:07:21,400 --> 00:07:24,140
Well, I don't know if concerned is the right word for it exactly.

111
00:07:24,680 --> 00:07:26,280
But ever since we got back from Italy,

112
00:07:26,900 --> 00:07:28,160
Maka's been acting all strange.

113
00:07:28,240 --> 00:07:29,580
I think something's been bothering her.

114
00:07:30,460 --> 00:07:30,860
Really?

115
00:07:30,860 --> 00:07:32,620
I'm sorry to hear that.

116
00:07:34,620 --> 00:07:37,520
A jar?

117
00:07:38,020 --> 00:07:39,100
That's right, a jar.

118
00:07:39,620 --> 00:07:40,780
Is it a special jar?

119
00:07:40,940 --> 00:07:41,880
Nope, nothing special.

120
00:07:41,980 --> 00:07:43,200
It's just an ordinary jar.

121
00:07:43,700 --> 00:07:46,640
Now, the water that's inside the jar is another story altogether.

122
00:07:47,240 --> 00:07:48,800
It's called soul-sapping water

123
00:07:48,800 --> 00:07:50,560
because it sucks out your soul wavelength.

124
00:07:51,520 --> 00:07:53,920
Compared to that, the jar's very ordinary indeed.

125
00:07:54,340 --> 00:07:56,180
Go on, try sticking your hand in the water.

126
00:07:56,180 --> 00:07:58,900
All right, but I'm still a little iffy about this jar.

127
00:08:03,440 --> 00:08:04,420
What was that?

128
00:08:04,700 --> 00:08:06,040
I knew that jar was dangerous.

129
00:08:06,420 --> 00:08:07,640
No, it's just the water.

130
00:08:08,220 --> 00:08:11,360
You might want to start off by sticking in only one finger at a time.

131
00:08:11,580 --> 00:08:14,720
All I have to do is get to where I can withstand putting my whole hand in there,

132
00:08:14,840 --> 00:08:17,700
and then I can use Tsubaki's enchanted sword mode, professor?

133
00:08:18,360 --> 00:08:19,640
That's the basic idea.

134
00:08:19,640 --> 00:08:21,600
That'll be a nice break.

135
00:08:21,900 --> 00:08:24,760
All I've been doing lately is muscle conditioning, and it's getting old.

136
00:08:25,140 --> 00:08:25,540
Huh?

137
00:08:26,260 --> 00:08:27,000
What's with you?

138
00:08:27,260 --> 00:08:28,060
It isn't fair.

139
00:08:28,400 --> 00:08:31,240
How can you get stronger just by playing with a jar filled with water?

140
00:08:31,540 --> 00:08:31,800
Ha!

141
00:08:31,960 --> 00:08:32,740
Isn't it obvious?

142
00:08:32,920 --> 00:08:33,940
I'm Blackstar.

143
00:08:34,140 --> 00:08:35,660
I'm on a whole different level than you.

144
00:08:35,840 --> 00:08:36,780
I'm a big man.

145
00:08:36,940 --> 00:08:37,840
I've beaten death.

146
00:08:38,060 --> 00:08:39,100
Who else can say that?

147
00:08:39,360 --> 00:08:40,260
No fair.

148
00:08:40,640 --> 00:08:43,200
Professor Stein, can I have one of those special jars, too?

149
00:08:43,660 --> 00:08:44,720
I can't do that.

150
00:08:45,260 --> 00:08:49,760
The water in the jar is only intended to help Blackstar be able to use Tsubaki's enchanted

151
00:08:49,760 --> 00:08:50,400
sword mode.

152
00:08:50,960 --> 00:08:53,120
I'm not going to let myself get beaten by a jar.

153
00:08:53,300 --> 00:08:54,700
I don't care how special it is.

154
00:08:55,040 --> 00:08:59,300
I'd be surprised if Blackstar even realized what he was doing by saying things like that.

155
00:08:59,480 --> 00:09:03,660
By talking constantly about what a star he is and how big he is, Blackstar is actually

156
00:09:03,660 --> 00:09:05,600
driving himself without even meaning to.

157
00:09:06,660 --> 00:09:07,500
Driving himself?

158
00:09:08,420 --> 00:09:08,860
Yes.

159
00:09:09,420 --> 00:09:11,160
There's no stage too big for me.

160
00:09:11,240 --> 00:09:12,200
Of course I can do it.

161
00:09:12,200 --> 00:09:14,660
But that's his answer to any challenge he faces.

162
00:09:15,740 --> 00:09:19,580
And once he's said that, he will put every effort into making it happen, because he's

163
00:09:19,580 --> 00:09:21,240
already decided he will succeed.

164
00:09:21,860 --> 00:09:23,720
Blackstar is trying to surpass death.

165
00:09:24,480 --> 00:09:26,140
He is bound to become stronger.

166
00:09:26,720 --> 00:09:27,140
Right.

167
00:09:27,640 --> 00:09:29,920
But that's his way of making himself stronger.

168
00:09:30,120 --> 00:09:32,100
It's not a method that will work for everybody.

169
00:09:32,640 --> 00:09:35,560
You have to find your own way to do it, something that works for you.

170
00:09:36,220 --> 00:09:37,960
My own way of becoming stronger?

171
00:09:38,260 --> 00:09:40,580
Right now you're definitely lacking something, Maka.

172
00:09:40,580 --> 00:09:46,020
A certain level of stress and anxiety is understandable, but you don't want to take it too far.

173
00:09:47,020 --> 00:09:48,700
Wait, what do you mean lacking something?

174
00:09:49,200 --> 00:09:52,860
Once you figure out what it is, come see me and we'll decide what to do about it.

175
00:09:54,320 --> 00:09:56,740
Didn't I tell you to start out with only one finger?

176
00:09:56,740 --> 00:09:59,020
You can take the jar with you.

177
00:09:59,080 --> 00:10:00,260
The lesson's over for now.

178
00:10:00,640 --> 00:10:02,500
Hey, Maka, what about the party?

179
00:10:02,840 --> 00:10:04,120
Oh, yeah, I almost forgot.

180
00:10:04,440 --> 00:10:08,340
I was going to throw a party to congratulate Tsubaki and Blackstar since they finally managed

181
00:10:08,340 --> 00:10:11,520
to collect a soul and to celebrate the fact that Soul's coming home.

182
00:10:12,080 --> 00:10:14,140
Be sure to have some good fish dishes, okay?

183
00:10:14,140 --> 00:10:17,540
He's strong, huh?

184
00:10:20,580 --> 00:10:21,380
Okay, soul.

185
00:10:21,580 --> 00:10:23,480
I expect to see you back here in one week.

186
00:10:25,820 --> 00:10:26,660
Excuse me.

187
00:10:28,400 --> 00:10:28,800
Hey.

188
00:10:28,800 --> 00:10:36,180
I'm going home to get ready for the party.

189
00:10:36,480 --> 00:10:37,140
See you there.

190
00:10:40,140 --> 00:10:41,880
Something does seem to be bothering her.

191
00:10:41,940 --> 00:10:42,540
Is it the scar?

192
00:10:43,440 --> 00:10:45,620
Yeah, that happens every time she sees it.

193
00:10:46,380 --> 00:10:48,020
She gets this pained look.

194
00:10:48,020 --> 00:11:04,940
Well, it may not have been tasty, but it sure was filling.

195
00:11:05,480 --> 00:11:06,520
Hey, I've got an idea.

196
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:08,360
Next time you do the cooking.

197
00:11:08,660 --> 00:11:09,960
Don't listen to him, Maka.

198
00:11:10,080 --> 00:11:10,820
It was delicious.

199
00:11:11,160 --> 00:11:12,060
Yum, yum.

200
00:11:12,380 --> 00:11:13,700
Yeah, thank you for the snacks.

201
00:11:13,820 --> 00:11:15,140
You guys have a nice place here.

202
00:11:15,200 --> 00:11:15,760
It's so tidy.

203
00:11:16,240 --> 00:11:17,780
You must make a point of keeping it clean.

204
00:11:17,780 --> 00:11:20,380
It helps that Maka yells at me whenever I make a mess.

205
00:11:20,800 --> 00:11:22,640
Is it just the two of you living here, then?

206
00:11:23,080 --> 00:11:23,700
Yoo-hoo!

207
00:11:23,880 --> 00:11:25,400
Is everyone having a good time?

208
00:11:25,980 --> 00:11:28,820
Which one of you little boys wants to come and take a bath with me?

209
00:11:28,880 --> 00:11:29,960
The water's nice and warm.

210
00:11:30,540 --> 00:11:37,320
Is it always like this over here?

211
00:11:37,700 --> 00:11:38,260
Oh, yeah.

212
00:11:38,740 --> 00:11:41,260
Anybody want to take the sexy kitty home, she's free.

213
00:11:47,780 --> 00:11:53,380
Infiltrating the academy was worth the risk.

214
00:11:53,380 --> 00:11:58,340
I'll need to run some tests on Sol now that he has Ragnarok's black blood inside him.

215
00:11:59,340 --> 00:12:01,240
With this key, it should be easy.

216
00:12:06,320 --> 00:12:09,880
Well, what a coincidence running into you here.

217
00:12:09,880 --> 00:12:12,920
Have you already guessed what we're doing here, Medusa?

218
00:12:13,980 --> 00:12:15,300
Or should I tell you?

219
00:12:15,800 --> 00:12:16,560
Oh, please.

220
00:12:16,840 --> 00:12:17,360
Tell me.

221
00:12:18,160 --> 00:12:18,800
Ribbit, ribbit.

222
00:12:19,160 --> 00:12:20,180
All right, then I will.

223
00:12:20,440 --> 00:12:21,920
We've come here to kill you.

224
00:12:21,920 --> 00:12:24,480
Oh, no, but that's terrible.

225
00:12:24,860 --> 00:12:25,980
I thought we were friends.

226
00:12:26,480 --> 00:12:27,580
Don't take it personally.

227
00:12:27,800 --> 00:12:31,040
We simply have no interest in attracting the attention of the Grim Reaper.

228
00:12:31,420 --> 00:12:35,160
And we don't care for whatever little experiments you're doing at the academy, either.

229
00:12:35,640 --> 00:12:37,220
You're now a liability, Medusa.

230
00:12:37,880 --> 00:12:39,600
And liabilities must be killed.

231
00:12:40,360 --> 00:12:43,920
Before you do that, though, may I offer you a little piece of advice?

232
00:12:44,500 --> 00:12:46,360
That outfit is a liability, too.

233
00:12:46,480 --> 00:12:48,020
It simply screams witch.

234
00:12:48,460 --> 00:12:54,980
Whether you're casting soul protect or not, there are a good number of young maesters wandering these streets who know a witch when they see one.

235
00:12:55,660 --> 00:12:57,940
Sweet of you to warn us, but don't you worry.

236
00:12:58,220 --> 00:13:03,280
If it comes to it, we can use our transformation magic to escape, which is a luxury you don't have.

237
00:13:04,300 --> 00:13:05,340
I see now.

238
00:13:05,740 --> 00:13:07,700
So that's how you're planning to beat me, is it?

239
00:13:08,200 --> 00:13:11,460
We know we couldn't beat you in a fight under ordinary circumstances.

240
00:13:11,460 --> 00:13:15,200
But here in Death City, you need to maintain your cover as a school nurse.

241
00:13:15,200 --> 00:13:18,300
You can't drop your soul protect and use magic to defend yourself.

242
00:13:18,680 --> 00:13:19,780
That would be a dead giveaway.

243
00:13:21,240 --> 00:13:22,260
You're cornered.

244
00:13:22,420 --> 00:13:25,080
All we have to do is attack you while you're using soul protect.

245
00:13:25,480 --> 00:13:27,640
If you don't fight back, we'll defeat you easily.

246
00:13:27,920 --> 00:13:32,580
And if you do release your soul protect to attack us, we'll transform and make a clean escape.

247
00:13:33,580 --> 00:13:37,320
Meanwhile, you'll be revealed to the maesters as a witch, and they'll hunt you down.

248
00:13:38,040 --> 00:13:40,060
Whatever you decide to do, we still win.

249
00:13:40,220 --> 00:13:41,800
Not a bad plan, wouldn't you say?

250
00:13:41,800 --> 00:13:44,580
And that's how the frog and mouse will beat the snake.

251
00:13:45,220 --> 00:13:47,220
Tonight, you'll be the one croaking, not me.

252
00:13:47,540 --> 00:13:48,940
Funny how the world works.

253
00:13:49,440 --> 00:13:53,160
